{"id":"n4-073","title":"Verb + 続ける","romaji":"つづける, tsuzukeru","jlptLevel":4,"shortExplanation":"To continue doing or to keep doing an action.","longExplanation":"The grammar point 続ける (tsuzukeru) is attached to the masu-stem form of verbs, and it indicates the ongoing continuity of an action. It can be translated as 'to continue doing' or 'to keep doing' in English.","formation":"Verb-masu-stem + 続ける","examples":[{"jp":"彼は二時間走り続けました。","romaji":"Kare wa nijikan hashiritsuzukemashita.","en":"He kept running for two hours.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"二","vocabId":"1461140","reading":"に"},{"surface":"時間","vocabId":"1315920","reading":"じかん"},{"surface":"走り","vocabId":"1402420","reading":"はしり","baseForm":"走る"},{"surface":"続け","vocabId":"1405800","reading":"つづける","baseForm":"続ける"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5]},{"jp":"雨が一日中降り続けている。","romaji":"Ame ga ichinichijuu furitsuzukete iru.","en":"It has kept raining all day.","words":[{"surface":"雨","vocabId":"1171900","reading":"あめ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"一日中","vocabId":"1165500","reading":"いちにちちゅう"},{"surface":"降り","vocabId":"1631470","reading":"ふり","baseForm":"降る"},{"surface":"続け","vocabId":"1405800","reading":"つづける","baseForm":"続ける"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"日本語を勉強し続けたいです。","romaji":"Nihongo o benkyou shitsuzuketai desu.","en":"I want to keep studying Japanese.","words":[{"surface":"日本語","vocabId":"1464530","reading":"にほんご"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"勉強","vocabId":"1512670","reading":"べんきょう"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"続け","vocabId":"1405800","reading":"つづける","baseForm":"続ける"},{"surface":"たい","vocabId":null},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patter